  "nameStory": "",
  "description": "The Northeastern Pebble Bee is a small, solitary bee species belonging to the Megachilidae family, characterized by its compact body and nesting habits in cavities and plant stems. These bees are important pollinators found throughout New England and play a vital role in native plant reproduction.",
